Training: The model makes predictions, computes loss, computes gradients (backprop), and updates weights. The model is learning and changing.
Evaluating: The model makes predictions on test data to measure performance, but no weight updates occur.
@torch.no_grad() is used during evaluation because we don't need gradients (no backprop/weight updates). It saves memory and computation by telling PyTorch not to track operations for gradient computation.
